P2.5          26182       10989   0.420 [0.420 0.421]         15193       14145   1.074

  Read the last column carefully. It is the core's own encode work, crossings
  included, against the whole managed control -- and on six of the eight payloads
  it is BELOW 1.0. The Rust codec plus the C ABI does the encoding faster than
  the C# codec does. What loses the arm is the column beside it.

  The subtraction has one caveat and it goes the other way: run on its own, the
  fill writes 308 KB (P2.2) that nothing then reads, so it keeps more of that in
  cache than it does inside a real encode. If anything the fill-only arm
  understates the fill's share.

